# Drømtorp Awards – Cursor Rules

## Project Identity
This is **IT-Gullruten / Drømtorp Awards** – a school awards voting platform built for Drømtorp videregående skole. The event runs from ~12:00–13:15 with 10 main categories, jury-based winners, and a public audience vote.

---

## Tech Stack (NEVER deviate from this)
- **Framework:** Next.js 15 (App Router)
- **Language:** TypeScript – strict mode always
- **Database:** Neon DB (PostgreSQL via `@neondatabase/serverless`)
- **Auth:** NextAuth.js v5 (Auth.js) with Email / Magic Link provider
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS v4 + CSS variables
- **Image hosting:** Cloudinary (external only – no SDK integration needed in the app)
- **Package manager:** `pnpm` ONLY – never suggest `npm install` or `yarn`
- **Runtime:** Node.js / Vercel Edge where appropriate

---

## Package Manager Rules
- ALWAYS use `pnpm` – never `npm install`, never `yarn add`
- Use `pnpx` only when running one-off CLI tools (e.g. `pnpx prisma`)
- Lock file is `pnpm-lock.yaml` – never delete it

---

## Design System – SACRED, NEVER CHANGE

### Color Palette
These exact hex values must be used as CSS variables. Do not invent new colors.

```css
:root {
  --color-gold:        #C9A84C; /* Prestige Gold – primary accent */
  --color-gold-light:  #E8D5A3; /* Mjuk Gull – background fields */
  --color-gold-deep:   #8B6914; /* Dyp Gull – shadows, depth */
  --color-black:       #1C1C1C; /* Obsidian Black – backgrounds, text */
  --color-charcoal:    #2D2D2D; /* Mørk Kull – secondary background */
  --color-parchment:   #FAF8F4; /* Pergament – light backgrounds */
  --color-white:       #FFFFFF; /* White – text on dark surfaces */
}
```

### Typography
Import from Google Fonts. Never substitute these fonts.

| Role | Font | Weight | Size |
|---|---|---|---|
| Display / Title | Cormorant Garamond | Light 300 | 56–72px |
| Heading 1 | Montserrat | SemiBold 600 | 28–36px |
| Heading 2 | Montserrat | Medium 500 | 20–24px |
| Body | Montserrat | Regular 400 | 10–12px |
| Caption | Montserrat | Light 300 Italic | 8–9px |

### Visual Style
- Dark-first: primary backgrounds use `--color-black` and `--color-charcoal`
- Gold accents on borders, highlights, buttons, and active states
- Light surfaces use `--color-parchment`
- All text on dark surfaces must be `--color-white` or `--color-gold-light`
- Buttons: gold background (`--color-gold`) with black text, or outlined gold on dark
- No gradients unless they blend between the defined palette
- Smooth transitions: `transition: all 0.2s ease`
- Rounded corners: `rounded-lg` (8px) as default

---

## File & Folder Structure

```
app/
  (auth)/login/
  (protected)/vote/ results/ admin/...
  api/auth/ votes/ categories/ nominees/ users/
components/
  ui/ layout/ voting/ admin/ results/
lib/
  db/ auth/ validations/ utils/
types/
  index.ts
auth.ts
middleware.ts
```

---

## Database – Neon DB Rules
- Use `@neondatabase/serverless` with the `neon()` tagged template literal
- All queries go in `lib/db/`
- Schema is raw SQL (no ORM) – keep a `schema.sql` at the root
- Use parameterized queries ALWAYS – never string interpolation in SQL
- Table names: `users`, `categories`, `nominees`, `votes`, `approved_emails`

### Core Schema Shape
```sql
-- approved_emails: predefined list set by admin
-- users: id, name, email, role (user|producer|admin), status (approved|pending|rejected), created_at
-- categories: id, name, description, is_active, created_at
-- nominees: id, name, category_id, image_url (Cloudinary URL stored as text), created_at
-- votes: id, user_id, category_id, nominee_id, created_at
-- UNIQUE constraint on (user_id, category_id) to prevent duplicate votes
```

---

## Authentication Rules
- Use NextAuth.js v5 (Auth.js) – Email magic link or credentials
- Session strategy: JWT
- On sign-in: check `approved_emails` table → if found, auto-approve; else mark as `pending`
- Protect routes via middleware (`middleware.ts`)
- Role checks: always server-side via `auth()` or session – never trust client-side role

---

## Role-Based Access
| Route | Roles Allowed |
|---|---|
| `/vote` | `approved` users only |
| `/results` | all authenticated users |
| `/admin/*` | `producer`, `admin` |
| `/admin/users` | `admin` only (manage roles) |

---

## Voting Rules (enforce server-side)
1. One vote per user per category – enforced by DB UNIQUE constraint
2. Only `approved` users can vote – check status on every vote API call
3. All votes server-action or API route – never client-side only
4. Return clear error if user has already voted in that category

---

