---

## Component Rules
- All components: TypeScript with explicit prop types
- Use `"use client"` only when strictly necessary (event handlers, browser APIs)
- Prefer Server Components by default
- Form submissions: use Next.js Server Actions
- Loading states: use `Suspense` + skeleton components
- Error states: always handle and display user-friendly messages

---

## Code Quality
- No `any` types – use `unknown` and narrow properly
- Zod for all form and API input validation
- `eslint` + `prettier` – follow the project config
- No unused imports or variables
- Comment non-obvious logic, but don't over-comment

---

## Naming Conventions
- Files/folders: `kebab-case`
- Components: `PascalCase`
- Functions/variables: `camelCase`
- DB columns: `snake_case`
- Constants: `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE`
- Types/Interfaces: `PascalCase`, prefix interfaces with `I` only if needed for clarity

---

## Do Not
- Do not use `npm` or `yarn` – pnpm only
- Do not change any color values
- Do not change the font families
- Do not use Prisma – raw SQL with Neon serverless driver
- Do not use `any` TypeScript type
- Do not store sensitive data in client components
- Do not skip server-side role/auth checks
- Do not use Cloudinary SDK – store image URLs as plain text from manual uploads
